# REQUIRES: python-api, hdf5, cuda
# An output leaves the run alone (#233) on a GPU: in the deterministic mode
# the run with `[output] observables`, the free-energy file, the pull file,
# an energy file, and a trajectory ends in the state of the run without
# them, bit for bit, with the rows of its log, under NPT with the barostat
# of Trotter type, in mixed precision. The same with `rebuild_interval`, and
# for the rows of the log at the end only (D204). A Python simulation whose
# parts are read between them, or that has reporters, ends in the state of
# one that is not read.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/output_independence.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide GPU mdir %t Mixed NPT-TROTTER | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: GPU Mixed NPT-TROTTER: {{[0-9]+}} builds of the neighbor structure in 40 steps
# CHECK-SAME: compared observables, free_energy, pull, files, interval-files, rows-at-end
# CHECK: GPU Mixed mdir run: the outputs leave the final state and the rows of the log as they are without them, in 1 ensembles
# CHECK: GPU Mixed Python: state() and view() between the parts and the reporters
# CHECK: output independence passed
